From: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: add hwmon support for RTL8261C/D

The RTL8261C/D family exposes the same thermal sensor block as the
RTL822x: TSALRM at VEND2 0xa662, TSRR at 0xbd84 as a signed 10-bit
half-degree Celsius value, and the downshift threshold at 0xb54c. The
Realtek vendor RTL8261CE driver reads the temperature from TSRR with
the same decode as rtl822x_hwmon_read().

Register the existing RTL822x hwmon device from rtl8261x_probe() so the
10G ports of the Gemtek W1700K keep reporting their PHY temperature
when they carry an RTL8261CE, as the RTL8261N does.

temp1_max is unverified on this family: the vendor driver decodes the
threshold from bit 7 of 0xb54c in whole degrees, the RTL822x helper
from bit 6 in half degrees.

Signed-off-by: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -449,6 +449,9 @@
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY_HWMON))
+		return rtl822x_hwmon_init(phydev);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
